ValeVision3D - object snap: the running modes, what a hit belongs to, and the grips' check

  The maths (the real Geometry unit)
  PASS  a perpendicular from (4, 7) lands on the line at (4, 0), four tenths of the way along
  PASS  ...and one from beyond the end lands on the LINE, off the SEGMENT (t above 1)
  PASS  a segment with no length has no perpendicular
  PASS  the nearest point on a segment is its end when the foot runs off it
  PASS  two diagonals cross in the middle
  PASS  a line that STOPS on another touches it, and that counts (a T junction)
  PASS  parallel lines never cross, overlapping or not
  PASS  lines that would cross beyond their ends do not
  PASS  a rectangle's centre of area is its middle
  PASS  an L-shaped room balances off the middle of its box, inside the L
  PASS  three points in a line have no area: the middle of the points
  PASS  a level line is filed under every square it runs through
  PASS  a plumb one likewise
  PASS  a line that only CLIPS the corner of a square is still filed under it (sampling along it misses this)
  PASS  a shallow diagonal names the squares it passes through and no others
  PASS  a steeper one: it climbs into the next row BEFORE it leaves the first column

  The switches (the real State unit)
  PASS  object snap starts on, as it always has
  PASS  Endpoint, Midpoint, Intersection, Perpendicular and Centre start on; Nearest starts OFF
  PASS  every kind of object starts in reach
  PASS  a mode and a target switched are remembered in this browser
  PASS  a config's defaults never override what the browser has chosen - only what it has not
  PASS  a name that is not a mode is refused
  PASS  F3 keeps the storage key it has always had

  The search (the real State, Geometry, Index, Sources and Search units)

    Endpoint and Midpoint, and what each hit belongs to
  PASS  the end of a wall line of the drawing: a square, the viewports' purple
  PASS  the corner of a vector: a square, the vectors' blue
  PASS  the middle of a vector's edge: a triangle
  PASS  the corner of a text box: the text's orange - text could not be snapped to before
  PASS  ...and the middle of its box: a centre
  PASS  a point a dimension measures: the dimensions' red
  PASS  a corner of the sheet's border: the paper's slate
  PASS  a line hidden by the frame offers nothing: its end is past the viewport's edge
  PASS  ...but where the frame CUTS it is not an endpoint either
  PASS  hidden lines stay out of it until the config asks for them

    Intersection
  PASS  the wall and the jamb cross at (200, 150) and share no endpoint: a cross, purple
  PASS  a construction line crossing the wall: neither search alone has both lines; the crossing is the sheet's blue
  PASS  where a crossing and an endpoint coincide, the endpoint's written-down coordinates win

    The drawing outranks a vector's copy of it
  PASS  a vector's vertex exactly on a corner of the drawing: the DRAWING's point is taken, and the marker is purple
  PASS  ...and one a hair off it (0.04 mm): still the drawing's corner, so the new point lands ON the wall, not on the copy
  PASS  ...but a vertex the drawing has no point near is the vector's own, and blue says so

    Perpendicular
  PASS  with nothing to be square FROM there is no perpendicular: the first point of a line
  PASS  a line drawn from (170, 110) meets the wall square on at (170, 150): a boxed right angle
  PASS  ...from anywhere: the foot is under the point it is drawn from, not under the cursor
  PASS  a foot that would land OFF the end of the wall is refused
  PASS  a vertex dragged between two neighbours may be square from EITHER of them
  PASS  square on to a VECTOR works the same: the room's top edge, from a point above it
  PASS  a corner beside the foot still wins: an endpoint outweighs a perpendicular

    Centre, and the Vector Tools' circles
  PASS  the centre of area of a closed vector: a circle
  PASS  a circle offers its centre
  PASS  ...and its four quadrant points, as endpoints
  PASS  ...but NOT a vertex every few millimetres round it (48 of them here)
  PASS  without the curve hint the same points are an ordinary polygon, and every vertex snaps

    Nearest
  PASS  off by default: a cursor beside the wall, away from any point, finds nothing
  PASS  switched on: the closest point on the wall, an hourglass
  PASS  ...but only when no other mode has a point in reach: an endpoint beside it still wins

    Switching modes and targets
  PASS  Midpoint off: the middle of an edge finds nothing
  PASS  Text out of reach: its corner finds nothing, while the vector beside it still snaps
  PASS  Viewport linework out of reach: the wall's end finds nothing, and there is nothing to carry the viewport by
  PASS  a viewport is carried by a point of its OWN linework
  PASS  the config's Endpoints switch still rules the mode out altogether, as before there was a menu
  PASS  F3 off: nothing at all

    What is left out
  PASS  a vertex in motion never snaps to itself, nor to the middles of the two edges it drags
  PASS  ...but the rest of its own vector is still there to close onto
  PASS  a vector moved whole leaves all of itself out
  PASS  a carried viewport leaves its own linework out
  PASS  a text item in a moved selection leaves itself out

    Snap, the marker and the grid
  PASS  Snap hands back the point, its kind and what it belongs to, and shows that marker
  PASS  nothing in reach: the point is its own and the marker goes
  PASS  Grid Snap on: the grid answers where no object snap reaches, in the grid's own colour
  PASS  ...unless the caller keeps steps of its own ({ grid : false })

    Overspill note regions: on the paper, like the notes margin
  PASS  a region's corner: a square, the paper's slate
  PASS  ...the middle of a side: a triangle
  PASS  ...its centre: a circle
  PASS  ...and square on to a side from a point above it: a boxed right angle
  PASS  a region being dragged never snaps to itself
  PASS  one hanging off the page offers where it is DRAWN, moved onto the page
  PASS  regions switched off offer nothing, kept or not
  PASS  ...nor does a sheet that is not the one on screen

  Is a vertex ON the drawing (OnLinework): green, a green ring, or blue
  PASS  exactly on the end of the wall: a point (solid green)
  PASS  exactly on its middle: a point
  PASS  where the wall and the jamb cross, which is no endpoint of either: still a point
  PASS  somewhere along the wall, at no particular place: a line (a green ring)
  PASS  a fraction of a millimetre off the wall - it only LOOKS as if it is on it: free (blue)
  PASS  on a vector, but not on the drawing: free. The check is about the DRAWING
  PASS  F3 and the running modes do not come into it: it is a check, not a snap
  PASS  a hidden viewport is not there to be on
  PASS  SegmentsInBox hands a trim or an extend the lines of the drawing a box touches, each once

  The glyphs (the real Glyphs unit)
  PASS  every kind of snap has a marker of its own
  PASS  every marker is drawn in currentColor over a white casing, so the stylesheet owns its colour
  PASS  every mode the menu lists has a picture, and the grid and the inferred line (which it does not list) have none

  Every check passed.
